<title>FRANCE: E. Europe states to get 4.5 bln Ecus EU farm aid.</title>
<headline>E. Europe states to get 4.5 bln Ecus EU farm aid.</headline>
<dateline>STRASBOURG, France 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eastern European countries joining the EU will receive 4.5 billion Ecus from EU agricultural funds by 2006, European Commission estimates showed.</p>
<p>This includes 0.5 million Ecus of pre-accession aid in 2000, rising to 0.6 million Ecus a year between 2002-2006.</p>
<p>Assuming that the first new members join in 2002, they will receive an additional 1.1 billion Ecus a year in market support and 0.6 million Ecus a year for rural development.</p>
<p>The aid will rise to 1.4 billion Ecus and 2.5 billion Ecus respectively by 2006.</p>
<p>The European Commission announced on Wednesday that it will open negotiations with a first wave of five eastern European countries -- Hungary, Poland, the Czech republic, Estonia and Slovenia.</p>
<p>Another five former communist countries -- Latvia, Lithuania, Romania, Bulgaria and Slovakia -- have also applied to join.</p>
</text>
